    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\nThe spec: *a new owner's `membershipLevel` cannot exceed one above the current maximum `membershipLevel` among their household members; with no existing household member no cap applies.*\n\n`membershipLevel` is a derived field produced entirely by `OwnerMapper` \u2014 the single point used for both the `POST` response and later `GET` reads \u2014 so I implemented the cap there, keeping POST and GET consistent with no schema or entity changes.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.membershipLevel(Owner)`** (`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`)\n- Extracted the raw points\u2192level logic into a private `uncappedLevel(Owner)`.\n- `membershipLevel` now replays the owner's household **in creation (id) order**, capping each member at one above the running maximum of the earlier members' already-capped levels. The first member (no earlier household member) is uncapped. An owner with no `householdId`/`id` is returned uncapped. This is well-founded (each owner depends only on strictly-earlier members), so there is no circular dependency, and it matches \"the maximum among members that existed at creation.\"\n\n## Required supporting fix\n\nThe new test (`AcceptanceTest.coreCapsLevelByHousehold`) creates **two owners in the same household** (same lastName + postcode) with distinct telephones/emails, and asserts both are created. That was blocked at creation by a contradiction already in the codebase:\n\n- `OwnerIdentityKey`'s javadoc and `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate` both document that same-household owners with *different telephones* are created (and merely flagged as soft duplicates) \u2014 but `CheckUniqueOwnerIdentity` had an extra branch rejecting **any** same-household owner (unless `sharesHousehold`), which made `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`'s main branch unreachable dead code.\n\nSince a household-based level ceiling is meaningless if a household can never hold more than one member, I reconciled `CheckUniqueOwnerIdentity` to reject only **exact `identityKey` duplicates** (`<telephone>|<email>|<householdId>`), matching the documented contract. Soft matches are still flagged by `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`.\n\nI also updated the now-stale `openapi.yml` descriptions for `identityKey` and `membershipLevel`.\n\n## Verification\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreCapsLevelByHousehold` passes; audit log shows the two household members getting levels 1 and 2 (2 \u2264 1+1).\n- Full `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nOne note for transparency: relaxing the household-duplicate rule is a behavioral change beyond the one-line spec, but it's required to make the provided test green and it resolves a pre-existing internal inconsistency rather than introducing a new one.",
